# Public API

## `certificateFor(domains, options?)`

- `domains`: `string | string[]`. Multi-domain → SAN cert; cache path is `san-<numericHash>` via `getStableDomainPath`.
- Single domain cache path is the domain name itself under `domains/`.
- Flow: ensure root CA → generate domain cert if missing → update hosts (unless skipped) → return buffers.

### Options

| Option | Effect |
|--------|--------|
| `getCaBuffer` | Add `ca: Buffer` (CA cert contents) |
| `getCaPath` | Add `caPath: string` (path to CA cert file) |
| `skipCertutilInstall` | Do not install NSS `certutil`; Firefox may use GUI wizard |
| `skipHostsFile` | Do not append to system hosts file |
| `ui` | Partial `UserInterface` merged onto defaults |

Return type is conditional on options via TypeScript mapped types (`IReturnData`).

## Other exports

- `hasCertificateFor` / `configuredDomains` / `removeDomain` — cache inspection and cleanup (domain files only; does not untrust CA).
- `uninstall` — remove CA from trust stores and delete config (best-effort).

## Domain cert generation

`generateDomainCertificate`: `openssl genrsa` → CSR (templated conf) → `openssl ca` signed with root CA credentials loaded via `withCertificateAuthorityCredentials` (temp key file, deleted after).

## Integrator UI hooks

Implement any subset of `UserInterface` in `user-interface.ts`: Windows encryption password, Chrome/Linux certutil warning, Firefox close/wizard prompts.
